WEBVTT

00:00:21.994 --> 00:00:23.427
Sammy!

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:25.327
Take your brother outside
as fast as you can!

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:26.427
Go!

00:00:29.161 --> 00:00:31.360
Dad's on a hunting trip.

00:00:31.393 --> 00:00:33.161
And he hasn't been home in a few days.

00:00:35.994 --> 00:00:38.293
This is dad's book.

00:00:38.327 --> 00:00:40.161
I think he wants us to
pick up where he left off -

00:00:40.194 --> 00:00:43.861
Saving people, hunting
things, the family business.

00:00:43.894 --> 00:00:46.927
I got to find dad. It's the
only think i can think about.

00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:54.094
Bethany: now i lay me down to sleep.

00:00:54.128 --> 00:00:56.293
I pray the lord my soul to keep.

00:00:56.327 --> 00:00:59.027
Thy angels watch me through the night

00:00:59.061 --> 00:01:01.794
And keep me safe till morning light.

00:01:01.827 --> 00:01:04.761
Amen.

00:01:12.460 --> 00:01:15.260
Night, monkeypuss.

00:01:15.293 --> 00:01:17.094
Daddy?

00:01:17.128 --> 00:01:19.161
Is mommy coming home?

00:01:22.761 --> 00:01:25.027
No, honey.

00:01:25.061 --> 00:01:28.128
She's spending the night at
the hospital with your sister.

00:01:28.161 --> 00:01:29.460
Hey.

00:01:29.494 --> 00:01:31.627
You sleep tight now.

00:03:25.977 --> 00:03:29.177
Dean: yeah, you probably
missed something.

00:03:29.210 --> 00:03:31.344
Dude, i ran lexisnexis,
local police reports,

00:03:31.377 --> 00:03:33.644
Newspapers
- I couldn't find a single red flag.

00:03:33.677 --> 00:03:35.744
Are you sure you got
the coordinates right?

00:03:35.778 --> 00:03:36.878
Yeah, i double-Checked.

00:03:36.910 --> 00:03:38.210
It's fitchburg, wisconsin.

00:03:38.244 --> 00:03:40.210
Dad wouldn't have sent us coordinates

00:03:40.244 --> 00:03:41.878
If it wasn't important, sammy.

00:03:41.910 --> 00:03:43.210
Well, i'm telling you, i looked,

00:03:43.244 --> 00:03:45.244
And all i could find was a
big, steamy pile of nothing.

00:03:45.277 --> 00:03:46.577
If dad's sending us
hunting for something,

00:03:46.611 --> 00:03:47.644
I don't know what.

00:03:47.677 --> 00:03:49.144
Well, maybe he's gonna meet us there.

00:03:49.177 --> 00:03:52.344
Yeah, 'cause he's been so
easy to find up to this point.

00:03:52.377 --> 00:03:54.544
You're a real smartass, you know that?

00:03:54.577 --> 00:03:55.910
Don't worry.

00:03:55.943 --> 00:03:58.310
I'm sure there's something
in fitchburg worth killing.

00:03:58.344 --> 00:04:00.544
Yeah? What makes you so sure?

00:04:00.577 --> 00:04:03.744
Because i'm the oldest,
which means i'm always right.

00:04:03.778 --> 00:04:06.477
No, it doesn't. It totally does.

00:04:23.110 --> 00:04:24.611
Well, the waitress thinks

00:04:24.644 --> 00:04:27.778
That the local freemasons
are up to something sneaky,

00:04:27.811 --> 00:04:29.077
But other than that,

00:04:29.110 --> 00:04:31.844
Nobody's heard about
anything weird going on.

00:04:31.878 --> 00:04:35.277
Dean, you got the time?

00:04:35.310 --> 00:04:37.577
10 after 4:00.

00:04:37.611 --> 00:04:39.177
Why?

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:42.344
What's wrong with this picture?

00:04:47.444 --> 00:04:50.677
School's out, isn't it?

00:04:50.711 --> 00:04:52.310
Yeah.

00:04:55.144 --> 00:04:56.811
So where is everybody?

00:04:56.844 --> 00:05:00.577
This place should be
crawling with kids right now.

00:05:14.344 --> 00:05:16.977
It sure is quiet out here.

00:05:17.010 --> 00:05:18.778
Yeah, it's a shame.

00:05:18.811 --> 00:05:20.077
Why is that?

00:05:20.110 --> 00:05:23.577
You know, kids getting
sick. It's a terrible thing.

00:05:23.611 --> 00:05:25.910
How many?

00:05:25.943 --> 00:05:30.444
Just five or six, but
serious, hospital serious.

00:05:30.477 --> 00:05:33.177
A lot of parents are
getting pretty anxious.

00:05:33.210 --> 00:05:34.744
They think it's catching.

00:05:48.477 --> 00:05:50.844
Dude, dude, i am not using this i.D.

00:05:50.878 --> 00:05:52.010
Why not?

00:05:52.043 --> 00:05:54.077
Because it says "bikini
inspector" on it.

00:05:54.110 --> 00:05:56.043
Don't worry. She won't look that close.

00:05:56.077 --> 00:05:57.844
Hell, she won't even ask to see it.

00:05:57.878 --> 00:05:59.210
It's all about confidence, sammy.

00:06:00.344 --> 00:06:02.144
Hi.

00:06:02.177 --> 00:06:05.110
I'm dr. Jerry kaplan,
center for disease control.

00:06:05.144 --> 00:06:07.244
Can i see some i.D.?

00:06:10.177 --> 00:06:12.411
Yeah, of course.

00:06:14.744 --> 00:06:17.644
Now, could you direct me
to the pediatrics ward?

00:06:17.677 --> 00:06:21.144
Okay, just go down that hall,
turn left, up the stairs.

00:06:21.177 --> 00:06:22.644
You'll see them.

00:06:22.677 --> 00:06:24.477
Right. Thank you.

00:06:24.511 --> 00:06:26.611
See? Told you it would work.

00:06:26.644 --> 00:06:29.411
Follow me. It's upstairs.

00:07:03.677 --> 00:07:05.010
Sam: dean.

00:07:14.344 --> 00:07:16.377
Thanks for seeing us, dr. Hydaker.

00:07:16.411 --> 00:07:18.277
Oh, i'm glad you guys are here.

00:07:18.310 --> 00:07:20.677
I was just about to call the cdc myself.

00:07:20.711 --> 00:07:22.444
How did you find out anyway?

00:07:22.477 --> 00:07:24.644
Oh, some g.P. - I
forget his name -

00:07:24.677 --> 00:07:27.677
He called atlanta and must
have beat you to the punch.

00:07:27.711 --> 00:07:30.477
So you say you got six cases so far?

00:07:30.511 --> 00:07:32.878
Yeah, in five weeks.

00:07:32.910 --> 00:07:35.411
At first i thought it
was bacterial pneumonia,

00:07:35.444 --> 00:07:36.544
Not that newsworthy.

00:07:36.577 --> 00:07:38.444
But now...

00:07:38.477 --> 00:07:40.611
Now, what?

00:07:40.644 --> 00:07:42.977
The kids aren't
responding to antibiotics.

00:07:43.010 --> 00:07:45.277
Their white-Cell
counts keep going down.

00:07:45.310 --> 00:07:48.010
Their immune systems just
aren't doing their job.

00:07:48.043 --> 00:07:50.844
It's like their bodies are wearing out.

00:07:50.878 --> 00:07:52.444
Betty: excuse me, dr. Hydaker.

00:07:52.477 --> 00:07:54.244
You ever see anything like this before?

00:07:54.277 --> 00:07:55.411
Never this severe.

00:07:55.444 --> 00:07:57.943
The way it spreads
- That's a new one for me.

00:07:57.977 --> 00:07:59.210
What do you mean?

00:07:59.244 --> 00:08:00.744
It works its way through families,

00:08:00.778 --> 00:08:03.977
But only the children,
one sibling after another.

00:08:04.010 --> 00:08:07.477
You mind if we interview
a few of the kids?

00:08:07.511 --> 00:08:09.644
They're not conscious.

00:08:09.677 --> 00:08:11.811
None of them?

00:08:11.844 --> 00:08:13.644
No.

00:08:13.677 --> 00:08:16.844
Can we talk to the parents?

00:08:18.277 --> 00:08:20.210
If you think it'll help.

00:08:20.244 --> 00:08:23.811
Yeah, yeah. Who was your
most recent admission?

00:08:23.844 --> 00:08:26.077
I should get back to my girls.

00:08:26.110 --> 00:08:27.344
We understand that,

00:08:27.377 --> 00:08:30.077
And we really appreciate
you talking to us.

00:08:30.110 --> 00:08:32.144
Now, you say mary's the oldest?

00:08:32.177 --> 00:08:33.377
13.

00:08:33.411 --> 00:08:35.577
Okay, and she came down
with it first, right?

00:08:35.611 --> 00:08:36.677
And then...

00:08:36.711 --> 00:08:38.844
Bethany the next night.

00:08:38.878 --> 00:08:40.744
Within 24 hours?

00:08:40.778 --> 00:08:43.511
I guess.

00:08:43.544 --> 00:08:46.611
Look, i already went through
all this with the doctor.

00:08:46.644 --> 00:08:48.644
Right. Just a few more
questions, if you don't mind.

00:08:48.677 --> 00:08:50.577
How do you think they caught pneumonia?

00:08:50.611 --> 00:08:52.778
Were they out in the
cold, anything like that?

00:08:52.811 --> 00:08:54.943
No, we think it was an open window.

00:08:54.977 --> 00:08:57.277
Both times?

00:08:57.310 --> 00:09:00.878
The first time, i don't really remember,

00:09:00.910 --> 00:09:02.444
But the second time for sure,

00:09:02.477 --> 00:09:05.477
And i know i closed it
before i put bethany to bed.

00:09:05.511 --> 00:09:07.010
So you think she opened it?

00:09:07.043 --> 00:09:09.577
It's a second-Story window, no ledge.

00:09:09.611 --> 00:09:11.177
No one else could have.

00:09:15.744 --> 00:09:18.310
You know this might not
be anything supernatural.

00:09:18.344 --> 00:09:19.943
It might just be pneumonia.

00:09:19.977 --> 00:09:22.210
Maybe. Or maybe something
opened that window.

00:09:22.244 --> 00:09:25.110
I don't know, man. Look, dad
sent us down here for a reason.

00:09:25.144 --> 00:09:27.444
I think we might be
barking up the right tree.

00:09:27.477 --> 00:09:28.544
I'll tell you one thing.

00:09:28.577 --> 00:09:29.544
What?

00:09:29.577 --> 00:09:31.310
That guy we just talked to -

00:09:31.344 --> 00:09:34.110
I'm betting it'll be a
while before he goes home.

00:09:43.744 --> 00:09:46.177
You got anything over there?

00:09:46.210 --> 00:09:47.878
No, nothing.

00:09:47.910 --> 00:09:51.244
Yeah, me neither.

00:10:01.878 --> 00:10:03.344
Hey, dean.

00:10:03.377 --> 00:10:05.110
Dean: yeah?

00:10:06.611 --> 00:10:11.377
You were right. It's not pneumonia.

00:10:15.144 --> 00:10:17.310
It's rotted.

00:10:21.244 --> 00:10:23.844
What the hell leaves
a handprint like that?

00:10:27.177 --> 00:10:28.910
<i>Man: cheetara.</i>

00:10:28.943 --> 00:10:30.110
<i>Woman: i am sorry to wake you,</i>

00:10:30.144 --> 00:10:31.544
<i>But jaga bids me to bring you to him.</i>

00:10:31.577 --> 00:10:33.577
John: all right.

00:10:34.611 --> 00:10:36.177
You know the drill, dean.

00:10:36.210 --> 00:10:38.511
If anyone calls, you don't pick up.

00:10:38.544 --> 00:10:41.878
If it's me, i'll ring
once and then call back.

00:10:41.910 --> 00:10:43.244
You got that?

00:10:43.277 --> 00:10:46.577
Mm-Hmm. Don't answer the phone
unless it rings once first.

00:10:46.611 --> 00:10:49.210
Come on, dude. Look alive.
This stuff's important.

00:10:49.244 --> 00:10:50.344
I know, it's just,

00:10:50.377 --> 00:10:52.811
We've done it like a million times,

00:10:52.844 --> 00:10:54.644
And you know i'm not stupid.

00:10:54.677 --> 00:10:56.811
I know you're not, but
it only takes one mistake.

00:10:56.844 --> 00:10:58.210
You got that?

00:10:58.244 --> 00:11:01.611
<i>It's important that he join
jaga on the flight deck.</i>

00:11:01.644 --> 00:11:04.210
All right, if i'm not
back sunday night...

00:11:04.244 --> 00:11:05.611
Call pastor jim.

00:11:07.943 --> 00:11:10.511
Lock the doors and
windows, close the shades,

00:11:10.544 --> 00:11:11.744
And most important -

00:11:11.778 --> 00:11:13.310
Watch out for sammy.

00:11:13.344 --> 00:11:15.677
<i>Responsible for lion-O's
welfare, snarf is.</i>

00:11:15.711 --> 00:11:16.943
I know.

00:11:16.977 --> 00:11:18.611
All right, if something
tries to bust in...

00:11:18.644 --> 00:11:21.611
Shoot first, ask questions later.

00:11:21.644 --> 00:11:23.744
That's my man.

00:11:27.711 --> 00:11:29.010
<i>What's up, jaga?</i>

00:11:29.043 --> 00:11:30.110
<i>Come closer.</i>

00:11:34.943 --> 00:11:37.611
<i>What's happening to her?</i>

00:11:39.544 --> 00:11:41.411
<i>What was that?</i>

00:11:41.444 --> 00:11:44.010
Dean: i know why dad sent us here.

00:11:48.744 --> 00:11:50.844
He's faced this thing before.

00:11:52.910 --> 00:11:56.778
He wants us to finish the job.

00:12:19.183 --> 00:12:20.884
So what the hell is a shtriga?

00:12:20.917 --> 00:12:22.817
It's kind of like a witch, i think.

00:12:22.851 --> 00:12:24.484
I don't know much about them.

00:12:24.517 --> 00:12:26.484
Well, i've never heard of it,

00:12:26.517 --> 00:12:28.517
And it's not in dad's journal.

00:12:28.550 --> 00:12:31.183
Dad hunted one in fort
douglas, wisconsin,

00:12:31.217 --> 00:12:32.651
About 16, 17 years ago.

00:12:32.684 --> 00:12:35.517
You were there. You don't remember? No.

00:12:35.550 --> 00:12:38.018
I guess he caught wind that
the thing's in fitchburg now

00:12:38.051 --> 00:12:39.517
And kicked us the coordinates.

00:12:39.550 --> 00:12:41.784
So wait, this... shtriga.

00:12:41.817 --> 00:12:43.751
Right, you think it's the
same one dad hunted before?

00:12:43.784 --> 00:12:46.283
Yeah, maybe.

00:12:46.317 --> 00:12:48.317
If dad went after it, why
is it still breathing air?

00:12:48.350 --> 00:12:49.484
Because it got away.

00:12:49.517 --> 00:12:50.617
Got away?

00:12:50.651 --> 00:12:52.018
Yeah, sammy, it happens.

00:12:52.051 --> 00:12:53.217
Not very often.

00:12:53.250 --> 00:12:54.517
I don't know what to tell you.

00:12:54.550 --> 00:12:56.384
Maybe dad didn't have
his wheaties that morning.

00:12:56.417 --> 00:12:58.217
What else do you remember?

00:12:58.250 --> 00:13:00.450
Nothing. I was a kid, all right?

00:13:10.217 --> 00:13:11.851
King or two queens?

00:13:11.884 --> 00:13:13.450
Two queens.

00:13:17.550 --> 00:13:19.118
Yeah, i bet.

00:13:19.150 --> 00:13:20.317
What'd you say?

00:13:20.350 --> 00:13:22.283
Nice car.

00:13:22.317 --> 00:13:24.450
Hi. Checking in?

00:13:24.484 --> 00:13:25.684
Yeah.

00:13:25.717 --> 00:13:29.250
Uh, do me a favor. Go get
your brother some dinner.

00:13:29.283 --> 00:13:31.051
I'm helping a guest.

00:13:34.684 --> 00:13:36.851
Two queens.

00:13:38.984 --> 00:13:40.283
Funny kid.

00:13:40.317 --> 00:13:42.150
Oh, yeah, he thinks so.

00:13:42.183 --> 00:13:43.917
Will that be cash or credit?

00:13:43.951 --> 00:13:45.550
Do you take mastercard? Mm-Hmm.

00:13:45.584 --> 00:13:46.584
Perfect.

00:13:46.617 --> 00:13:47.684
There you go.

00:13:47.717 --> 00:13:50.118
Thank you.

00:14:05.984 --> 00:14:08.584
When's dad gonna get back?

00:14:08.617 --> 00:14:10.118
Tomorrow.

00:14:10.150 --> 00:14:11.350
When?

00:14:11.384 --> 00:14:12.384
I don't know.

00:14:12.417 --> 00:14:14.250
He usually comes in late, though.

00:14:14.283 --> 00:14:16.018
Now, eat your dinner.

00:14:16.051 --> 00:14:18.283
I'm sick of "scabetti-Os."

00:14:18.317 --> 00:14:20.917
Well, you're the one who wanted them.

00:14:20.951 --> 00:14:22.350
I want lucky charms.

00:14:22.384 --> 00:14:23.951
There's no more lucky charms.

00:14:23.984 --> 00:14:25.250
I saw the box.

00:14:25.283 --> 00:14:26.550
Okay, maybe there is,

00:14:26.584 --> 00:14:29.150
But there's only enough
left for one bowl,

00:14:29.183 --> 00:14:30.751
And i haven't had any yet.

00:14:54.517 --> 00:14:56.951
Do you want the prize?

00:14:56.984 --> 00:14:59.384
Sir?

00:15:01.183 --> 00:15:03.217
Thanks.

00:15:13.851 --> 00:15:15.517
Well, you were right.

00:15:15.550 --> 00:15:19.283
It wasn't very easy to
find, but you were right.

00:15:19.317 --> 00:15:21.784
A shtriga is a kind of witch.

00:15:21.817 --> 00:15:23.051
They're albanian,

00:15:23.084 --> 00:15:26.018
But legends about them
date back to ancient rome.

00:15:26.051 --> 00:15:28.118
They feed off of spiritus vitae.

00:15:28.150 --> 00:15:29.784
Spirit what?

00:15:29.817 --> 00:15:31.084
Vitae. It's latin.

00:15:31.118 --> 00:15:33.183
It translates to "breath of life,"

00:15:33.217 --> 00:15:36.517
Kind of like your life force or essence.

00:15:36.550 --> 00:15:38.517
Didn't the doctor say the
kids' bodies were wearing out?

00:15:38.550 --> 00:15:40.484
It's a thought.

00:15:40.517 --> 00:15:41.951
You know, she takes your vitality,

00:15:41.984 --> 00:15:44.118
Maybe your immunity goes to
hell, pneumonia takes hold.

00:15:44.150 --> 00:15:47.350
Anyway, shtrigas can feed
off anyone, but they prefer -

00:15:47.384 --> 00:15:49.118
Children.

00:15:49.150 --> 00:15:50.384
Yeah.

00:15:50.417 --> 00:15:52.484
Probably because they
have stronger life force.

00:15:52.517 --> 00:15:56.118
And get this
- Shtrigas are invulnerable

00:15:56.150 --> 00:15:58.717
To all weapons devised by god and man.

00:15:58.751 --> 00:16:00.951
No, that's not right.

00:16:00.984 --> 00:16:04.450
She's vulnerable when she feeds.

00:16:04.484 --> 00:16:05.484
What?

00:16:05.517 --> 00:16:07.450
If you catch her when she's eating,

00:16:07.484 --> 00:16:10.018
You can blast her with
consecrated wrought irons,

00:16:10.051 --> 00:16:11.884
Buckshots or rounds i think.

00:16:11.917 --> 00:16:13.550
How do you know that?

00:16:13.584 --> 00:16:16.384
Dad told me. I remember.

00:16:16.417 --> 00:16:18.817
Oh.

00:16:18.851 --> 00:16:22.884
So, uh, anything else
dad might have mentioned?

00:16:22.917 --> 00:16:25.217
No, that's it.

00:16:27.283 --> 00:16:29.384
What?

00:16:31.450 --> 00:16:33.417
Nothing.

00:16:33.450 --> 00:16:37.250
Okay, so, assuming we
can kill it when it eats,

00:16:37.283 --> 00:16:39.084
We've still got to find the thing first,

00:16:39.118 --> 00:16:40.617
Which ain't gonna be a cakewalk.

00:16:40.651 --> 00:16:43.051
Shtrigas take on a human
disguise when they're not hunting.

00:16:43.084 --> 00:16:44.751
What kind of human disguise?

00:16:44.784 --> 00:16:46.584
Historically, something innocuous.

00:16:46.617 --> 00:16:49.417
It could be anything, but it's
usually a feeble old woman,

00:16:49.450 --> 00:16:52.450
Which may be how the witches-As-
Old-Crones legend got started.

00:16:52.484 --> 00:16:53.550
Hang on.

00:16:53.584 --> 00:16:54.651
What?

00:16:56.651 --> 00:16:57.884
Check this out.

00:16:57.917 --> 00:17:00.084
I marked down all the
addresses of the victims.

00:17:00.118 --> 00:17:02.118
Now, these are the houses
that have been hit so far,

00:17:02.150 --> 00:17:03.350
And dead center -

00:17:03.384 --> 00:17:05.584
The hospital.

00:17:05.617 --> 00:17:08.751
When we were there, i saw
a patient, an old woman.

00:17:08.784 --> 00:17:10.183
An old person, huh?

00:17:10.217 --> 00:17:11.250
Yeah.

00:17:11.283 --> 00:17:12.350
In the hospital?

00:17:12.384 --> 00:17:14.417
Whew! Better call the coast guard.

00:17:14.450 --> 00:17:15.751
Well, listen, smartass,

00:17:15.784 --> 00:17:18.417
She had an inverted
cross hanging on her wall.

00:17:33.484 --> 00:17:35.651
Betty: good night, dr. Hydaker.

00:17:35.684 --> 00:17:37.217
See you tomorrow, betty.

00:17:37.250 --> 00:17:39.350
Try to get some sleep, aaron.

00:17:45.384 --> 00:17:46.784
Come on.

00:18:48.183 --> 00:18:50.384
Who the hell are you?

00:18:50.417 --> 00:18:51.684
Who's there?

00:18:53.817 --> 00:18:55.951
You trying to steal my stuff?

00:18:55.984 --> 00:18:57.851
They're always stealing around here.

00:18:57.884 --> 00:19:00.684
No, ma'am, we're
maintenance. We're sorry.

00:19:00.717 --> 00:19:02.317
We thought you were sleeping.

00:19:02.350 --> 00:19:04.051
Ah, nonsense.

00:19:04.084 --> 00:19:06.384
I was sleeping with my peepers open.

00:19:09.851 --> 00:19:12.817
And fix that crucifix, would you?

00:19:12.851 --> 00:19:16.317
I've asked four damn times already.

00:20:13.707 --> 00:20:17.007
"I was sleeping with my peepers open."

00:20:17.041 --> 00:20:20.341
I almost smoked that old gal, i swear.

00:20:20.374 --> 00:20:21.774
It's not funny.

00:20:22.801 --> 00:20:25.034
Oh, man, you should have
seen your face, dean.

00:20:25.067 --> 00:20:27.667
Oh, yeah, laugh it on, man.
We're back to square one.

00:20:30.234 --> 00:20:32.933
Hang on.

00:20:41.567 --> 00:20:44.200
Hey, what's wrong?

00:20:44.234 --> 00:20:47.134
My brother's sick.

00:20:47.167 --> 00:20:48.301
The little guy?

00:20:48.334 --> 00:20:50.200
Pneumonia.

00:20:50.234 --> 00:20:52.668
He's in the hospital.

00:20:54.067 --> 00:20:55.800
It's my fault.

00:20:55.833 --> 00:20:57.501
No, come on. How?

00:20:58.668 --> 00:21:01.267
I should have made sure
the window was latched.

00:21:01.301 --> 00:21:03.501
He wouldn't have gotten pneumonia

00:21:03.534 --> 00:21:05.167
If the window was latched.

00:21:09.000 --> 00:21:11.167
Listen to me.

00:21:11.200 --> 00:21:15.634
I can promise you that this
is not your fault, okay?

00:21:15.668 --> 00:21:18.100
It's my job to look after him.

00:21:24.933 --> 00:21:26.334
Michael.

00:21:28.768 --> 00:21:31.334
Turn on the "no vacancy"
sign while i'm gone.

00:21:31.367 --> 00:21:33.100
I've got denise covering room service,

00:21:33.134 --> 00:21:34.200
So don't bother with the rooms.

00:21:34.234 --> 00:21:35.567
I'm going with you. Not now, michael.

00:21:35.601 --> 00:21:36.701
But i got to see asher.

00:21:36.734 --> 00:21:38.167
Dean: hey, michael.

00:21:38.200 --> 00:21:39.534
Hey.

00:21:39.567 --> 00:21:42.334
I know how you feel.
I'm a big brother, too.

00:21:42.367 --> 00:21:45.067
But you got to go easy on
your mom right now, okay?

00:21:45.100 --> 00:21:46.267
Aw, damn it.

00:21:46.301 --> 00:21:47.567
I got it.

00:21:47.601 --> 00:21:50.334
Thanks. You're in no condition to drive.

00:21:50.367 --> 00:21:53.100
Why don't you let me give
you a lift to the hospital?

00:21:53.134 --> 00:21:54.434
No, no, i couldn't possibly -

00:21:54.467 --> 00:21:58.067
No, no trouble. I insist.

00:22:04.200 --> 00:22:06.000
Be good.

00:22:12.668 --> 00:22:14.401
We're gonna kill this thing.

00:22:14.434 --> 00:22:16.501
I want it dead. You hear me?

00:22:35.100 --> 00:22:36.134
Dean: hey.

00:22:36.167 --> 00:22:37.567
Hey, how's the kid?

00:22:37.601 --> 00:22:40.034
He's not good. Where you at?

00:22:40.067 --> 00:22:41.601
I'm at the library,

00:22:41.634 --> 00:22:44.167
Trying to find out as much
as i can about this shtriga.

00:22:44.200 --> 00:22:45.833
Yeah, what do you got?

00:22:45.867 --> 00:22:47.067
Well, bad news.

00:22:47.100 --> 00:22:49.301
I started with fort douglas

00:22:49.334 --> 00:22:51.501
Around the time you said dad was there.

00:22:51.534 --> 00:22:52.768
And?

00:22:52.800 --> 00:22:53.933
Same deal.

00:22:53.967 --> 00:22:57.334
Before that, there was ogdenville.

00:22:57.367 --> 00:23:01.234
Before that, north
haverbrook and brockway.

00:23:01.267 --> 00:23:04.967
Every 15 to 20 years,
it hits a new town.

00:23:05.000 --> 00:23:08.434
Dean, this thing is just
getting started in fitchburg.

00:23:08.467 --> 00:23:11.367
In all these other places,
it goes on for months,

00:23:11.401 --> 00:23:14.501
Dozens of kids, before the
shtriga finally moves on.

00:23:14.534 --> 00:23:18.100
Kids just languish in
comas, and then they die.

00:23:18.134 --> 00:23:20.301
How far back does this thing go?

00:23:20.334 --> 00:23:21.467
I don't know.

00:23:21.501 --> 00:23:24.167
The earliest mention i
could find is this place

00:23:24.200 --> 00:23:26.668
Called black river
falls back in the 1890s.

00:23:26.701 --> 00:23:29.501
Talk about a horror show.

00:23:31.234 --> 00:23:33.501
Whoa.

00:23:33.534 --> 00:23:34.534
Sam?

00:23:34.567 --> 00:23:36.000
Hold on.

00:23:36.034 --> 00:23:38.367
I'm looking at a photograph right now

00:23:38.401 --> 00:23:41.601
Of a bunch of doctors
standing around a kid's bed.

00:23:41.634 --> 00:23:44.501
One of the doctors is hydaker.

00:23:44.534 --> 00:23:46.067
And?

00:23:46.100 --> 00:23:49.334
And this picture was taken in 1893.

00:23:49.367 --> 00:23:51.534
You sure?

00:23:51.567 --> 00:23:53.134
Yeah.

00:23:53.167 --> 00:23:55.634
Yeah, absolutely.

00:24:14.134 --> 00:24:18.334
Don't worry. Your son's in good hands.

00:24:18.367 --> 00:24:21.601
I'm gonna take care of him.

00:24:21.634 --> 00:24:24.567
So what's the cdc come up with so far?

00:24:24.601 --> 00:24:27.100
We're still working on a few theories.

00:24:27.134 --> 00:24:29.701
You'll know something as soon as we do.

00:24:29.734 --> 00:24:33.167
Well, nothing's more important
to me than these kids.

00:24:33.200 --> 00:24:34.167
Hmm.

00:24:34.200 --> 00:24:36.534
Just let me know if i can help.

00:24:36.567 --> 00:24:39.768
I'll do that.

00:24:42.100 --> 00:24:44.534
Sam: we should have
thought of this before.

00:24:44.567 --> 00:24:47.000
Doctor's a perfect
disguise. You're trusted.

00:24:47.034 --> 00:24:48.900
You can control the whole thing.

00:24:48.933 --> 00:24:52.933
Huh. That son of a bitch.

00:24:52.967 --> 00:24:55.000
I'm surprised you didn't
draw on him right there.

00:24:55.034 --> 00:24:58.000
Yeah, well...

00:24:58.034 --> 00:25:00.000
First of all,

00:25:00.034 --> 00:25:01.967
I'm not gonna open fire in
a freakin' pediatrics ward.

00:25:02.000 --> 00:25:03.668
Good call.

00:25:03.701 --> 00:25:05.267
Second, it wouldn't have done any good

00:25:05.301 --> 00:25:06.668
Because the bastard's bulletproof

00:25:06.701 --> 00:25:08.267
Unless he's chowing down on something.

00:25:08.301 --> 00:25:09.501
And third, i wasn't packing,

00:25:09.534 --> 00:25:11.067
Which is probably a really good thing

00:25:11.100 --> 00:25:13.200
'Cause i probably would have
just burned a clip in him

00:25:13.234 --> 00:25:14.634
Off of principle alone.

00:25:14.668 --> 00:25:17.234
You're getting wise
in your old age, dean.

00:25:17.267 --> 00:25:18.467
You're damn right.

00:25:18.501 --> 00:25:21.100
'Cause now i know how
we're gonna get it.

00:25:21.134 --> 00:25:23.134
What do you mean?

00:25:23.167 --> 00:25:25.000
The shtriga
- It works through siblings, right?

00:25:25.034 --> 00:25:26.134
Right.

00:25:26.167 --> 00:25:27.534
Well, last night...

00:25:27.567 --> 00:25:28.768
It went after asher.

00:25:28.800 --> 00:25:30.701
Tonight it's probably
gonna come after michael.

00:25:30.734 --> 00:25:31.867
Then we got to get him out of here.

00:25:31.900 --> 00:25:34.167
No. No, that would blow the whole deal.

00:25:34.200 --> 00:25:35.668
What? Yeah.

00:25:35.701 --> 00:25:38.100
Then you want to use the kid as bait?

00:25:39.167 --> 00:25:41.933
Are you nuts? No. Forget it.
That's out of the question.

00:25:41.967 --> 00:25:44.467
Sam, it's the only way
- If this thing disappears,

00:25:44.501 --> 00:25:46.800
It could be years before
we get another chance.

00:25:46.833 --> 00:25:48.567
Michael's a kid, and
i'm not gonna dangle him

00:25:48.601 --> 00:25:50.334
In front of that thing
like a worm on a hook.

00:25:50.367 --> 00:25:52.334
Dad did not send me here to walk away.

00:25:52.367 --> 00:25:54.534
<i>Send you here? He didn't send you here.</i>

00:25:54.567 --> 00:25:56.768
<i>He sent us here. This
isn't about you, sam.</i>

00:25:56.800 --> 00:25:58.601
I'm the one that screwed
up. It's my fault.

00:25:58.634 --> 00:26:00.701
There's no telling how
many kids have gotten hurt

00:26:00.734 --> 00:26:01.833
Because of me.

00:26:01.867 --> 00:26:05.434
What are you saying,
dean? How is it your fault?

00:26:11.234 --> 00:26:12.668
Dean.

00:26:12.701 --> 00:26:15.933
You've been hiding
something from the get-Go.

00:26:15.967 --> 00:26:18.601
Since when does dad bail on a hunt?

00:26:18.634 --> 00:26:21.668
Since when does he
let something get away?

00:26:21.701 --> 00:26:26.900
Now, talk to me, man.
Tell me what's going on.

00:26:36.467 --> 00:26:39.234
Fort douglas, wisconsin.

00:26:39.267 --> 00:26:42.267
It was the third night
in this crap room,

00:26:42.301 --> 00:26:44.900
And i was climbing the walls, man.

00:26:44.933 --> 00:26:46.734
I needed to get some air.

00:26:46.768 --> 00:26:48.367
<i>...if ever i saw one.</i>

00:26:48.401 --> 00:26:50.000
<i>Command performance.</i>

00:27:16.933 --> 00:27:18.267
Hey, kid.

00:27:19.434 --> 00:27:21.434
We're closing up.

00:28:24.833 --> 00:28:26.134
Get out of the way!

00:28:36.467 --> 00:28:40.701
Sammy. Sammy. Sammy.

00:28:40.734 --> 00:28:42.000
You okay?

00:28:42.034 --> 00:28:44.768
Sam: dad, what's going on?

00:28:44.800 --> 00:28:46.634
Are you all right?

00:28:50.234 --> 00:28:53.634
What happened?

00:28:53.668 --> 00:28:55.701
I
- I just went out.

00:28:55.734 --> 00:28:57.401
What?

00:28:57.434 --> 00:29:00.067
J
- Just for a second. I'm sorry.

00:29:00.100 --> 00:29:02.467
I told you not to leave this room.

00:29:02.501 --> 00:29:05.467
I told you not to let
him out of your sight.

00:29:17.668 --> 00:29:21.933
Dad just grabbed us and booked,

00:29:21.967 --> 00:29:27.501
Dropped us off at pastor
jim's about three hours away.

00:29:27.534 --> 00:29:30.301
By the time he got back to fort douglas,

00:29:30.334 --> 00:29:32.200
The shtriga had disappeared.

00:29:32.234 --> 00:29:34.467
It was just gone.

00:29:37.501 --> 00:29:41.668
It never resurfaced until now.

00:29:41.701 --> 00:29:44.668
Dad never spoke about it again.

00:29:44.701 --> 00:29:47.701
I didn't ask.

00:29:47.734 --> 00:29:50.234
But he, uh...

00:29:52.401 --> 00:29:57.501
He looked at me different,
you know, which was worse.

00:29:57.534 --> 00:29:59.000
Not that i blame him.

00:29:59.034 --> 00:30:01.900
He gave me an order,
and i didn't listen,

00:30:01.933 --> 00:30:04.067
And i almost got you killed.

00:30:04.100 --> 00:30:05.501
You were just a kid.

00:30:05.534 --> 00:30:09.501
Don't.

00:30:09.534 --> 00:30:14.034
Dad knew this was
unfinished business for me.

00:30:14.067 --> 00:30:17.267
He sent me here to finish it.

00:30:19.334 --> 00:30:23.134
But using michael
- I don't know, dean.

00:30:23.167 --> 00:30:26.367
I mean, how about one of
us hides under the cover?

00:30:26.401 --> 00:30:29.267
You know, we'll be the bait.

00:30:29.301 --> 00:30:32.267
No, that won't work.

00:30:32.301 --> 00:30:35.301
It's got to get close
enough to feed. It'll see us.

00:30:37.867 --> 00:30:40.367
Believe me, i don't like it,
but it's got to be the kid.

00:30:45.967 --> 00:30:47.933
Michael: you're crazy!

00:30:47.967 --> 00:30:50.567
Just go away or i'm calling the cops.

00:30:50.601 --> 00:30:52.634
Hang on a second. Just listen to me.

00:30:52.668 --> 00:30:55.134
You have to believe me, okay?

00:30:55.167 --> 00:30:56.734
This thing came through the window

00:30:56.768 --> 00:30:57.933
And attacked your brother.

00:31:00.501 --> 00:31:01.567
I've seen it.

00:31:01.601 --> 00:31:03.100
I know what it looks like

00:31:03.134 --> 00:31:05.601
'Cause it attacked my brother once, too.

00:31:12.833 --> 00:31:14.768
This thing -

00:31:14.800 --> 00:31:17.434
Is it, like...

00:31:17.467 --> 00:31:22.000
It has this long, black robe?

00:31:22.034 --> 00:31:24.267
You saw it last night, didn't you?

00:31:24.301 --> 00:31:28.267
I thought i was having a nightmare.

00:31:30.334 --> 00:31:34.301
I'd give anything not to tell you this,

00:31:34.334 --> 00:31:36.401
But sometimes nightmares are real.

00:31:36.434 --> 00:31:39.534
<i>So why are you telling me?</i>

00:31:39.567 --> 00:31:41.334
Because we need your help.

00:31:41.367 --> 00:31:42.734
My help?

00:31:42.768 --> 00:31:47.501
We can kill it, me and
him. It's what we do.

00:31:47.534 --> 00:31:49.567
But we can't do it without you.

00:31:49.601 --> 00:31:52.800
What? No.

00:31:52.833 --> 00:31:54.534
Michael, listen to me.

00:31:54.567 --> 00:31:56.301
This thing hurt asher,

00:31:56.334 --> 00:31:59.534
And it's gonna keep hurting
kids unless we stop it.

00:31:59.567 --> 00:32:01.000
Do you understand me?

00:32:03.701 --> 00:32:06.634
Well, that went crappy. Now what?

00:32:06.668 --> 00:32:07.833
What did you expect?

00:32:07.867 --> 00:32:10.434
You can't ask an adult
to do something like that,

00:32:10.467 --> 00:32:12.167
Much less a kid.

00:32:20.401 --> 00:32:23.234
If you kill it, will asher get better?

00:32:28.034 --> 00:32:31.567
Honestly, we don't know.

00:32:34.601 --> 00:32:37.501
You said you're a big brother.

00:32:37.534 --> 00:32:39.734
Yeah.

00:32:39.768 --> 00:32:41.601
You'd take care of your little brother?

00:32:41.634 --> 00:32:45.467
You'd do anything for him?

00:32:45.501 --> 00:32:47.734
Yeah, i would.

00:32:49.634 --> 00:32:53.434
Me too.

00:32:53.467 --> 00:32:54.833
I'll help.

00:33:15.970 --> 00:33:17.604
This camera has night vision on it,

00:33:17.638 --> 00:33:19.638
So we'll be able to
see you as clear as day.

00:33:19.670 --> 00:33:20.870
Are we good?

00:33:20.904 --> 00:33:22.037
Hair to the right.

00:33:22.070 --> 00:33:23.970
There, there.

00:33:24.004 --> 00:33:27.271
Michael: what do i do?

00:33:27.304 --> 00:33:30.904
Just stay under the covers.

00:33:30.937 --> 00:33:34.437
And if it shows up?

00:33:34.471 --> 00:33:36.337
Well, we'll be right in the next room.

00:33:36.371 --> 00:33:38.937
We're gonna come in with
guns, so as soon as we do,

00:33:38.970 --> 00:33:41.304
You roll off this bed
and you crawl under it.

00:33:43.371 --> 00:33:45.104
What if you shoot me?

00:33:45.137 --> 00:33:47.703
We won't shoot you. We're good shots.

00:33:49.337 --> 00:33:52.571
We're not gonna fire
until you're clear, okay?

00:33:52.604 --> 00:33:55.070
Have you heard a gunshot before?

00:33:55.104 --> 00:33:56.737
Like in the movies?

00:33:56.770 --> 00:34:00.337
It's gonna be a lot
louder than in the movies.

00:34:00.371 --> 00:34:03.970
So i want you to stay under
the bed, cover your ears,

00:34:04.004 --> 00:34:07.237
And do not come out until
we say so, you understand?

00:34:10.004 --> 00:34:12.837
Michael, are you sure
you want to do this?

00:34:12.870 --> 00:34:14.604
You don't have to. It's
okay. I won't be mad.

00:34:14.638 --> 00:34:16.638
No, i'm okay.

00:34:16.670 --> 00:34:19.471
Just don't shoot me.

00:34:19.504 --> 00:34:22.737
We're not gonna let
anything happen to you.

00:34:22.770 --> 00:34:24.070
I promise.

00:34:36.870 --> 00:34:38.237
What time is it?

00:34:40.337 --> 00:34:41.504
3:00.

00:34:43.538 --> 00:34:45.371
You sure these iron
rounds are gonna work?

00:34:47.337 --> 00:34:48.770
Consecrated iron rounds.

00:34:48.803 --> 00:34:52.437
And yeah, it's what dad used last time.

00:34:52.471 --> 00:34:55.171
Hey, dean, i'm sorry.

00:34:58.004 --> 00:34:59.070
For what?

00:35:01.703 --> 00:35:03.604
You know...

00:35:03.638 --> 00:35:06.737
I've really given you a lot of crap

00:35:06.770 --> 00:35:10.304
For always following dad's orders,

00:35:10.337 --> 00:35:13.803
But i know why you do it.

00:35:13.837 --> 00:35:15.837
Oh, god. Kill me now.

00:35:21.104 --> 00:35:22.171
Wait, look.

00:35:56.970 --> 00:35:58.604
Now? Not yet.

00:36:33.070 --> 00:36:34.604
Michael, down!

00:36:44.770 --> 00:36:46.471
Mike, you all right? Yeah.

00:36:46.504 --> 00:36:49.204
Just sit tight.

00:37:11.670 --> 00:37:12.703
Dean!

00:37:43.137 --> 00:37:45.037
Dean: hey!

00:37:48.137 --> 00:37:49.937
You okay, little brother?

00:38:22.504 --> 00:38:24.437
It's okay, michael. You can come on out.

00:38:56.977 --> 00:38:59.044
Hey, joanna, how's asher doing?

00:38:59.077 --> 00:39:01.111
Have you seen michael?
Michael: mom! Mom!

00:39:01.144 --> 00:39:02.744
Hey!

00:39:04.244 --> 00:39:05.443
How's ash?

00:39:05.477 --> 00:39:07.577
I've got some good news.
Your brother's gonna be fine.

00:39:07.610 --> 00:39:08.777
Really?

00:39:08.810 --> 00:39:10.777
Yeah, really. No one can explain it.

00:39:10.810 --> 00:39:13.644
It's, uh, it's a miracle.

00:39:13.677 --> 00:39:15.810
They're gonna keep him in
overnight for observation,

00:39:15.844 --> 00:39:17.311
But after that, he's coming home.

00:39:17.344 --> 00:39:18.378
That's great.

00:39:18.410 --> 00:39:20.911
How are all the other kids doing?

00:39:20.944 --> 00:39:22.144
Good, real good.

00:39:22.177 --> 00:39:24.244
A bunch of them should be
checking out in a few days.

00:39:24.278 --> 00:39:26.777
Dr. Travis says the ward's
gonna be like a ghost town.

00:39:26.810 --> 00:39:30.044
Dr. Travis? What about dr. Hydaker?

00:39:30.077 --> 00:39:31.144
Oh, he wasn't in today.

00:39:31.177 --> 00:39:32.877
He must have been sick or something.

00:39:32.911 --> 00:39:35.443
Yeah, yeah, must have.

00:39:35.477 --> 00:39:39.610
So did anything happen while i was gone?

00:39:39.644 --> 00:39:41.610
No, same old stuff.

00:39:41.644 --> 00:39:43.410
Okay. You can go see ash.

00:39:43.443 --> 00:39:44.944
Now? Only if you want to.

00:39:49.543 --> 00:39:50.810
I better get going

00:39:50.844 --> 00:39:53.077
Before he hot-Wires the
car and drives himself.

00:39:59.610 --> 00:40:03.311
It's too bad.

00:40:03.344 --> 00:40:05.944
No, they'll be fine.

00:40:05.977 --> 00:40:07.344
